00:01:06.782 --> 00:01:08.222
I don’t want to be called an actor.

00:01:08.222 --> 00:01:09.372
I don’t want to be called a star.

00:01:09.622 --> 00:01:10.772
I don’t want to have a label.

00:01:11.288 --> 00:01:13.258
I want to have a legacy.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:19.790
I want to be known as someone who has goals and achieves them,

00:01:19.916 --> 00:01:22.746
And whatever they might be,
wherever they might be.

00:01:22.986 --> 00:01:24.365
I want to be limitless.

00:01:24.635 --> 00:01:26.785
I want to breake stereotypes

00:01:26.888 --> 00:01:30.368
I want to go where no man or woman has gone before.

00:01:30.462 --> 00:01:32.572
And it might be a scary path

00:01:32.572 --> 00:01:34.452
And it might be a path that no one's taken,

00:01:34.452 --> 00:01:35.952
But at least it'll be just mine.

00:01:40.139 --> 00:01:43.239
I had the worst self-esteem when I was a kid

00:01:43.864 --> 00:01:46.974
I was made fun of because of the way I talked,

00:01:46.974 --> 00:01:48.404
Because of where I came from,

00:01:48.404 --> 00:01:50.414
I was made fun of on every level

00:01:50.472 --> 00:01:55.662
And the only way you can change that is setting goals for yourself, and saying

00:01:55.712 --> 00:01:57.712
"I'll be the best version of me."

00:01:58.286 --> 00:02:00.696
When I was 18 and I started doing movies

00:02:00.847 --> 00:02:04.017
I gave myself a year and a half. And I said, if I don't;

00:02:04.194 --> 00:02:06.224
If I sense that I'm not good at what I'm doing

00:02:06.224 --> 00:02:09.714
And I don't see something opening up for me,

00:02:10.075 --> 00:02:11.415
I'm going to go back to college.

00:02:11.415 --> 00:02:12.735
I always had a plan B

00:02:12.735 --> 00:02:14.305
I still always have a plan B.

00:02:14.305 --> 00:02:15.765
And that's what I always tell young people, that

00:02:15.765 --> 00:02:19.675
You know, life doesn't end, it just keeps moving.

00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:21.515
You have to put your blinkers on

00:02:21.515 --> 00:02:23.955
And find what you do best and just keep moving.

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:29.743
America suddenly sat up and said ‘Oh’, this is a great business module.

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:33.582
To take an international superstar and put them into something

00:02:33.842 --> 00:02:35.672
and that just elevates the popularity.

00:02:35.672 --> 00:02:38.022
Because today it’s not just about the domestic entertainment,

00:02:38.132 --> 00:02:39.282
it’s global.

00:02:40.042 --> 00:02:41.612
So now everyone wants that.

00:02:41.739 --> 00:02:44.039
But the women, because we’re beautiful.

00:02:44.579 --> 00:02:45.429
-That you are.

00:02:46.156 --> 00:02:48.386
And the “exotic, beautiful, Indian girl”,

00:02:49.516 --> 00:02:52.556
it’s an easier fit.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.355
I’ve gone to the left and decided never to do it.

00:02:55.639 --> 00:02:57.999
Because I did a show which is on my shoulders,

00:02:57.999 --> 00:03:00.839
I’m doing a movie in which I’m not the side chick,

00:03:01.472 --> 00:03:03.672
I’m the main villain of the movie,

00:03:03.742 --> 00:03:04.682
which is different.

00:03:04.732 --> 00:03:05.995
Who would debut as a 
villain?

00:03:06.295 --> 00:03:08.665
My first debut will be a villain,

00:03:08.795 --> 00:03:09.455
an antagonist.

00:03:09.626 --> 00:03:11.456
But to me, that strikes me as exciting.

00:03:11.836 --> 00:03:13.626
I don’t like being conventional.

00:03:13.654 --> 00:03:16.054
But I was tried to put into that box so much.

00:03:16.324 --> 00:03:17.793
That was the first place I was put into.

00:03:17.793 --> 00:03:19.613
All the movies that came to me was that.

00:03:20.259 --> 00:03:23.709
In fact Baywatch, I was being spoken to for another 
part.

00:03:25.139 --> 00:03:27.729
And it was written for a man, that I told you last time

00:03:27.993 --> 00:03:31.123
So, I like my terms a little bit

00:03:31.149 --> 00:03:40.309
But the exotic, gorgeous, pretty girl in amazing clothes is so the fit of where people tried to put me.

00:03:40.809 --> 00:03:42.709
And I hope that doesn’t happen to anyone else coming in

00:03:42.773 --> 00:03:45.413
Because it’ll really ruin all the work I’ve done.

00:03:47.283 --> 00:03:51.453
So you’re like on the phone; "Deepika, let me just lay down the rules here”.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:54.176
No, no, no, everyone can do what they want.

00:03:54.256 --> 00:03:57.626
We need to stand as a force to reckon with
because our industry is that.

00:03:57.796 --> 00:04:01.146
Our industry is one of the most prolific in the world.

00:04:01.293 --> 00:04:06.563
And we need to not be afraid to stand our ground on our feet and say, “I’m not settling”.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.976
And I hope that Indian talent comes in and do that.

00:04:08.976 --> 00:04:14.156
And I hope that me being in the position that I am in can give them the confidence to do it.

00:04:14.258 --> 00:04:16.028
I've never known my life without movies,

00:04:16.069 --> 00:04:19.799
I don't know what that would be like and now I'm doing music too in the last.

00:04:19.799 --> 00:04:22.939
I mean I made an albume I've almost 40 songs ready

00:04:22.939 --> 00:04:25.589
In the last tow years and I've finished 8 movies.

00:04:25.625 --> 00:04:29.105
So I've been able to ... 
-I'm sorry Superwomen where is your cape?

00:04:29.658 --> 00:04:33.068
-I'm sorry what's going on?
You do you sleep?

00:04:33.282 --> 00:04:35.842
I do, I do, but I do worked everyday

00:04:35.909 --> 00:04:39.419
I love what I do, and I have tow careers that I have 
to handle right now,

00:04:39.419 --> 00:04:42.029
And I don't want to give up on 
either on of them and I don't think I need to.

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:44.550
-Do you feel like if you don't work you go crazy?

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.360
I think so

00:04:45.512 --> 00:04:48.512
-Like no I can't take because feel like .....

00:04:48.512 --> 00:04:53.232
I've been working like the since I was 17 
I don't know how to do anything else

00:04:53.232 --> 00:04:55.682
And I haven't found a reason to want to take
a break yet,

00:04:55.691 --> 00:04:56.741
If you know what I mean

00:04:57.531 --> 00:05:02.581
"My name is Alex Parrish, protecting our country
had always my dream"

00:05:03.495 --> 00:05:05.095
Quantico's my first audition,

00:05:05.101 --> 00:05:11.211
I knew I had to go in to this room
and read these lines in front of all these people,

00:05:11.387 --> 00:05:13.367
But I was so nervous before I went in,

00:05:13.517 --> 00:05:16.097
So I went to the bathroom, I remember, 
before I went in,

00:05:16.097 --> 00:05:19.307
And looked in the mirror and it's so stupid and cliche,

00:05:19.626 --> 00:05:22.636
I talked to myself, and I said, "What's wrong with you?"

00:05:22.827 --> 00:05:28.367
"You've played the most difficult characters in
the most complicated movies"

00:05:28.573 --> 00:05:32.573
I tossed my hair a little bit, felt great, and walked out.

00:05:34.349 --> 00:05:37.109
Did my bit, and got the job.

00:05:37.149 --> 00:05:40.369
Priyanka, do you as an actor have any lines
in your head

00:05:40.369 --> 00:05:42.509
In terms of what you will do and won’t do?

00:05:42.739 --> 00:05:43.929
Yea, nudity.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.267
For sure, I wouldn’t do it.

00:05:45.419 --> 00:05:46.279
Like never.

00:05:50.362 --> 00:05:53.882
I play bold parts.
But

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.350
I don’t like a lot of skin show.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.370
I don’t know how to explain it.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:03.490
Like in "Aitraaz", I was always in pantsuits.

00:06:03.747 --> 00:06:07.327
But the intensity and the part was sexual,
I didn't have to dress it.

00:06:07.477 --> 00:06:09.157
You don’t have to dress provocatively.

00:06:09.157 --> 00:06:11.657
Yea. I mean I would do it for a magazine cover here and there

00:06:11.664 --> 00:06:13.544
Because it’s glamorous and its pretty.

00:06:14.084 --> 00:06:16.504
Like one of the big reasons why I did the show

00:06:16.504 --> 00:06:18.164
With ABC was because they're Disney

00:06:18.638 --> 00:06:21.338
So there’s only that much for American standards

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:23.260
That we can do on the show

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:26.250
Which is pretty much as much as Hindi films.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:32.880
There’s a difference between wearing a bikini and a bra
and I understand that.

00:06:33.603 --> 00:06:36.323
And those lines are important to me.

00:06:36.792 --> 00:06:41.062
It's a very conscious effort for me to do something that 
challenges me every year.

00:06:41.246 --> 00:06:42.996
I do one of those but,

00:06:43.199 --> 00:06:45.939
I also do those where I can put my hair down
and just look pretty.

00:06:45.939 --> 00:06:47.279
I'm a girl I love doing it.

00:06:47.629 --> 00:06:51.279
I love blockbuster Hindi movies it's my favorite genre of film

00:06:51.694 --> 00:06:53.654
Whether it's in Hollywood or in Bollywood.

00:06:53.654 --> 00:06:54.784
You take me for an 'x-man';

00:06:54.887 --> 00:06:59.647
I would much rather go see that than I would see a film which tells me a serious story,

00:06:59.729 --> 00:07:00.699
I'm that audience.

00:07:01.039 --> 00:07:05.249
Yeah sometimes I feel as an actor I don't get pushed and challenged as much

00:07:05.518 --> 00:07:07.908
But you can't always be doing the same thing.

00:07:08.603 --> 00:07:11.613
I like the Will Smith way of doing movies.

00:07:12.028 --> 00:07:15.308
You do these big movies with big money and big budgets

00:07:15.308 --> 00:07:16.788
And they are commercial
and they are successful

00:07:16.788 --> 00:07:19.008
And look hot and you look great 
and then you do that.

00:07:19.527 --> 00:07:21.967
So you have to be able balance both.

00:07:21.967 --> 00:07:23.617
Very few actors get to do it.

00:07:23.617 --> 00:07:27.617
And I'm glad that I'm a part of that elite group of people.

00:07:28.008 --> 00:07:31.178
I don't consider myself a singer 
I don't consider myself an actor

00:07:31.489 --> 00:07:33.029
I consider myself an achiever.

00:07:33.029 --> 00:07:33.569
-Ok

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:34.750
You give me anything,

00:07:34.773 --> 00:07:36.833
You'll tell me to paint the walls of the studio

00:07:36.833 --> 00:07:38.963
And I'll do the best damn painting job
you've ever seen.

00:07:39.003 --> 00:07:39.475
-Ok

00:07:39.475 --> 00:07:40.805
That's how I've always been

00:07:40.805 --> 00:07:42.655
I didn't know I was gonna be an actress
-Right

00:07:42.655 --> 00:07:43.925
I didn't know I was gonna be a musician

00:07:44.303 --> 00:07:46.543
But now, whatever opportunities I get

00:07:46.543 --> 00:07:49.873
I trying turn them to "Let's see what will happened"
-Sure

00:07:50.108 --> 00:07:52.788
Hard work is something i know i can damn well do 
-Ok

00:07:52.897 --> 00:07:56.897
So I do that ...... alright I'll try something else.

00:07:57.125 --> 00:08:00.925
But I want to expand myself as an entertainer as a performer

00:08:00.925 --> 00:08:02.615
Whether that's music, whether that's tv

00:08:02.615 --> 00:08:06.195
Whether that's films, whether that's production, anything.

00:08:06.254 --> 00:08:10.384
It is now, Priyanka, 8 o’ clock.
You just finished shooting

00:08:10.384 --> 00:08:12.394
And now you’re heading to a party.

00:08:13.056 --> 00:08:16.436
I’m heading to the launch of
of the magazine

00:08:16.436 --> 00:08:20.336
Which is the W Magazine which is having a party for the launch of its Royals issue.

00:08:20.756 --> 00:08:24.696
I’m on their covers,
so I’m heading their now, yes.

00:08:25.317 --> 00:08:26.847
Kill me!

00:08:28.615 --> 00:08:33.955
You don’t look like
you’re feeling a ‘Kill Me!’ moment.

00:08:34.079 --> 00:08:36.399
How do you do that?
That’s never the debate Anu.

00:08:36.399 --> 00:08:38.739
That’s why people don’t think I’m ever tired.

00:08:39.349 --> 00:08:40.569
So how do you do this?

00:08:40.569 --> 00:08:42.749
How do you will yourself
into not being tired?

00:08:42.863 --> 00:08:46.113
It’s only because all the stuff that I have to do is what I need to do.

00:08:46.113 --> 00:08:48.963
I don’t have time for unnecessary work between two continents.

00:08:50.873 --> 00:08:53.933
My word is my bond.
It’s my commitment

00:08:55.286 --> 00:08:56.296
I’m professional.

00:08:56.296 --> 00:08:58.726
My inherent nature is that

00:08:58.726 --> 00:09:03.066
You have to keep working if you’re committed to something.

00:09:03.398 --> 00:09:05.518
So you’re tired,
but when you step out of this car

00:09:05.518 --> 00:09:08.658
It’s going to be
the million dollar smile.

00:09:09.056 --> 00:09:11.756
No one will know.
That's the thing.

00:09:12.724 --> 00:09:14.414
My mum used to say this to me.

00:09:14.734 --> 00:09:18.154
As a woman, no one should see the chinks in your armour

00:09:19.041 --> 00:09:20.511
Because it is only your own.

00:09:21.603 --> 00:09:25.603
We’re strong because
we have the ability as women

00:09:25.698 --> 00:09:32.918
To be able to hold on to a lot of emotional, a lot of things that are thrown at us.

00:09:35.064 --> 00:09:39.524
But we just have to remember that,
don’t let the world see your weakness.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:43.380
The most beautiful thing about having dreams is

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.760
That it's in your hands how big your dreams become.

00:09:46.281 --> 00:09:47.861
And this film taught me that.

00:09:48.441 --> 00:09:52.691
I've come here only to intoduce you to the idea of saying that

00:09:52.691 --> 00:09:58.791
No one can tell you that your dream is too small! or your dream can't come true

00:09:59.004 --> 00:10:02.474
Or your dream can't be allowed because you're a girl because you're a boy

00:10:02.474 --> 00:10:07.054
Because you look a certain way
or because you come from a certain place.

00:10:07.912 --> 00:10:10.892
I'm not even know this turn and I'm playing Mary Kom

00:10:10.999 --> 00:10:12.369
I mean who would thought that.

00:10:13.037 --> 00:10:16.387
I'm extremely honored to be sitting in front of all of you

00:10:16.387 --> 00:10:19.437
Wonderful wonderful really smart people and talking to you

00:10:19.437 --> 00:10:21.887
About my dream which came true
doing this film.

00:10:22.425 --> 00:10:26.275
Don't be afraid to dream guys because they do come true, they really do.

00:10:26.647 --> 00:10:27.807
When I was very young,

00:10:27.807 --> 00:10:29.917
I was 19 and I was doing
the first few movies,

00:10:30.189 --> 00:10:31.869
I remember the producer just 
said,

00:10:31.869 --> 00:10:34.609
"Well, if she can't work it out, it's fine,
we'll just cast someone else."

00:10:34.609 --> 00:10:35.829
"Girls are replaceable."

00:10:35.943 --> 00:10:38.523
Subconsciously, it really worked on my mind

00:10:38.803 --> 00:10:43.723
And I started picking up parts which were strong

00:10:43.822 --> 00:10:48.482
Which were not just the damsel in distress waiting for someone to rescue me.

00:10:48.666 --> 00:10:52.166
Now 13-15 years later, the movies I do

00:10:53.306 --> 00:10:54.626
I'm irreplaceable.

00:10:54.864 --> 00:10:56.124
Thank you guys so much for watching

